{"chapter": "cotangent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "08PQ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$P_n$", "MATH_0002": "$\\epsilon$", "MATH_0003": "$\\epsilon$", "MATH_0004": "$\\epsilon$", "PROOFARGEND_0001": "]\n", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-identify-pi-shriek}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{simplicial-lemma-standard-simplicial-homotopy}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{simplicial-lemma-homotopy-equivalence}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{simplicial-lemma-qis-simplicial-abelian-groups}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}[", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f450dde5fe2e65801b6db88c64f44676a2ef791089e430657824e50584200f2f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a2edfe2c6166347d3e29b8a19536ffdb7170cd98645688d806538c5a587922c4", "source_text": "First proof<PROOFARGEND_0001>We will apply Lemma <REF_0001>.\nSince the terms <MATH_0001> are polynomial algebras we see the first\nassumption of that lemma is satisfied. The second assumption is proved\nas follows. By\nSimplicial, Lemma <REF_0002>\nthe map <MATH_0002> is a homotopy equivalence of underlying\nsimplicial sets. By\nSimplicial, Lemma <REF_0003>\nthis implies <MATH_0003> induces a quasi-isomorphism of associated\ncomplexes of abelian groups. By\nSimplicial, Lemma <REF_0004>\nthis implies that <MATH_0004> is a trivial Kan fibration of underlying\nsimplicial sets.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c9ce2f6a969f8b7842df3345744d5bcecc4a6059fb5bc5d9ea4df7d6b9285dcb", "unit_id": "tag:08PT:proof"}
